From e4d4d62a158a980f997ec04a38f84a81de2478eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: onlyfish <linotfish@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:56:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] audiopolicy: cache Sony HAL state reads and coalesce
 notifications

AudioPolicyManager asks the HAL for Dolby/DSEE/360RA state several times per
startOutput()/getOutputForAttributes() (sonyDolbyEnabled alone can issue three
getParameters calls, sonyUsesDseeRouting a few more), and each read is a
synchronous HIDL round trip executed while AudioPolicyService_Mutex is held.
A slow HAL therefore delays the whole AudioPolicyService and can trip its
TimeCheck.

- Add a 200 ms TTL cache for Sony HAL parameter reads
  (sonyGetHalParamCached/Bool/Int), invalidated when we push a new state.
- Coalesce identical 360ra_contents notifications within 500 ms instead of
  sending a synchronous parametersCommand for every startOutput().
- Cache uid -> package name lookups: resolving it takes a PermissionController
  binder call plus a /data/system/packages.list scan.
- Dedupe the DSEE codec-client notification (AudioSystem::setParameters blocks
  MediaCodec configure).
- Downgrade per-stream Sony logs to ALOGV.

Change-Id: Ie3d7b7998cee5232685e48c5d0dac1ac90d3e20b
